WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.920
Get ready to ugly cry, Marvel fans.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:07.020
And beware, major Avengers: Infinity War spoilers
ahead.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.860
Guardians of the Galaxy director James Gunn
has shared a heart-shattering detail about

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.340
Groot in Infinity War that has has people
absolutely reeling.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.539
On Twitter, Gunn revealed the tree-like Guardian's
final line in the film, uttered just after

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:24.060
Josh Brolin's Thanos snaps his Infinity Gauntlet-rocking
hand to get rid of half the universe's population.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.640
Groot, voiced by Fast and the Furious franchise
star Vin Diesel, was one of the heroes that

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:33.469
disintegrated into a flurry of ashy space
bits, joined by a number of others, including

00:00:33.469 --> 00:00:38.030
Chadwick Boseman's Black Panther, Benedict
Cumberbatch's Doctor Strange, Elizabeth Olsen's

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:42.600
Scarlet Witch, and Tom Holland's Spider-Man,
who had what was largely considered the most

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.019
agonizing and tear-inducing final moment in
Infinity War.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:47.129
Until now.

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:49.199
"I am Groot."

00:00:49.199 --> 00:00:54.199
A fan asked Gunn on Twitter, "Might be too
soon to ask this, but do you know what Groot's

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:56.600
last line is at the end of the movie?"

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.140
Surprisingly, Gunn answered quickly and candidly,
disclosing that Groot's last word was "Dad,"

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:05.190
in reference to Bradley Cooper's Rocket Racoon.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:09.080
We are Groot, we are broken, and we're not
alone.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.550
One Twitter user responded to Gunn: "That
Groot and Rocket scene devastated my heart

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:14.550
and soul.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.790
I have NEVER imagined a time where a talking
tree calling a talking raccoon dad would be

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.510
this much, unironically, sad.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.510
Marvel what have you done to us."

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:27.152
When asked about it, Gunn reiterated that
the line was in the screenplay and that he

00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:29.700
didn't make up the answer to the fan on the
spot.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.460
The script in question is the exclusive "Groot
version" that only goes to Gunn and Diesel,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.580
so we'll have to take the director's tweet
reveal at face value.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:41.460
While Avengers: Infinity War continues to
blaze through box office records, recently

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.430
passing the $1 billion milestone in record
time, we'll be quietly sobbing in the corner

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.430
about all this.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.430
Thanks for watching!

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:50.910
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.560
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

